# Feature AI Prompt Coverage (mandatory — never skip)

**A feature is NOT shippable until AI can handle it on every surface where users interact with it.**

## Pipe-1 target flow (mandatory stages)

Every new AI feature must follow the confidence-gated understanding pipeline — see `ai-command-pipeline.mdc` for file-level detail:

`normalize → fast heuristics → LLM classify → confidence gate → (low: semantic + re-rank + optional narrow re-classify) → rescue → self-verify → structural enrich → validate → execute → telemetry`

Map your work to stages: classifier rules (classify), rescue fixtures (rescue), validators (validate), handlers (execute), eval cases (telemetry + accuracy). Do not bypass the pipeline with one-off classify/rescue shortcuts.

## Required surfaces (all four — never skip one)

| Surface | Users | Classifier schema | Service |
|---------|-------|-------------------|---------|
| **Dashboard admin** | Owner, manager, receptionist | `INTENT_SCHEMA` in `ai-command.service.ts` | `AiCommandService` |
| **Service provider mobile** | Stylists, staff on provider app | `PROVIDER_INTENT_SCHEMA` in `provider-ai-command.service.ts` | `ProviderAiCommandService` |
| **Customer mobile** | Logged-in customers on consumer app | `buildCustomerClassifierSchema()` in `customer-ai-command.util.ts` | `CustomerAiCommandService` (`surface: customer`) |
| **Public booking web** | Anonymous visitors on booking page | `buildPublicClassifierSchema()` in `public-booking-assistant.service.ts` | `PublicBookingAssistantService` |

If a feature ships on only some surfaces, document which are out of scope — but **never assume dashboard-only**. Provider mobile, customer mobile, and public booking each need their own prompts when the feature is user-visible there.

## Definition of done

Before marking a feature complete, verify ALL of the following **per applicable surface**:

1. **Classifier rules** — shared constants in `*.fixtures.ts` (see `ai-check-and-book.fixtures.ts`):
   - `*_CLASSIFIER_RULES` → dashboard `INTENT_SCHEMA` + customer `buildCustomerClassifierSchema()`
   - `PROVIDER_*_CLASSIFIER_RULES` → `PROVIDER_INTENT_SCHEMA` (+ `buildProviderClassifierAppendix()` when needed)
   - `PUBLIC_*_CLASSIFIER_RULES` → `buildPublicClassifierSchema()`
   - Per-surface action names differ — duplicate rules with correct verbs (e.g. dashboard `create_booking` / `check_providers_for_service`, public `book_appointment` / `check_availability`, provider `mark_paid` / `list_my_bookings`)

2. **99% UX scenario coverage** — natural-language variants real users say on that surface:
   - Happy path, synonyms, edge phrasing (quotes, semicolons, "then", questions)
   - Mobile-appropriate phrasing (shorter prompts, voice-to-text quirks, tap-to-suggest wording)
   - Export as `SIMILAR_*_PROMPTS` or `*_SCENARIOS` in fixtures with `id`, `prompt`, `surface`, expected params

3. **Multi-command compounds** — when the feature composes with others:
   - Decomposition in `*.util.ts` per surface (`decompose*CompoundPrompt`, `decomposeDeterministicForSurface`)
   - 2-step and 3+ step flows; shared context across steps
   - Provider and customer mobile compounds tested separately (action names differ)

4. **Post-LLM rescue** — deterministic fallback when classifier mislabels:
   - Dashboard/customer: `AiIntentRescueService`, `rescuePaymentsIntent`, `enrich*FromPrompt`
   - Provider mobile: provider-specific rescue in `provider-ai-*.util.ts`
   - Public booking: rescue paths in `public-booking-assistant.service.ts`

5. **Eval golden cases** — add per-surface entries to `eval/ai-command-eval.cases.ts` (`npm run test:sprint14`); tag `surface: dashboard | provider | customer | public`

## Agent workflow (blocking)

When implementing or reviewing ANY feature:

- [ ] List which of the **four surfaces** expose this feature
- [ ] Add classifier rules wired into **each** applicable schema (not dashboard-only)
- [ ] Add ≥10 NL prompt variants **per surface** (provider mobile + customer mobile + public booking when applicable)
- [ ] Add compound decomposition per surface if multi-step is possible
- [ ] Add rescue + heuristic enrichment per surface
- [ ] Add eval cases with correct `surface` tag
- [ ] **Do not mark TODO `[x]` or say "done" without this checklist**

Reference: `ai-cmd-h1` — `ai-check-and-book.fixtures.ts` (dashboard/customer/public rules), `ai-payments.util.ts`, `ai-check-and-book.integration.spec.ts`, `public-booking-assistant.schema.spec.ts`, `customer-ai-command.util.spec.ts`.

